We also apply a known periodic separable $(1,2,1)/4$ smoothing filter followed by column scales increasing from 0.5 to 2, before masking and centering. In 300 fresh-reference trials, matched upper-tail $H_u$ rejects 12 times (0.040), while references omitting the extra map reject all 300. This is a controlled correlated/heteroscedastic added-noise scenario covered by the fixed-map rank principle. The projector moment formulas are not invoked for this non-projector map; neither the map nor its covariance is estimated from the tested image.
